      },
      "worked": "Let the axial intercepts be $(u,0)$ and $(0,v)$. Their midpoint is $(a,b)$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac u2&=a\\\\u&=2a\\\\\\frac v2&=b\\\\v&=2b.\\end{align*}$$\nA standard-form line through $(2a,0)$ and $(0,2b)$ is $bx+ay=2ab$: substituting either intercept gives $2ab$ on the left. Therefore, the required equation is $bx+ay=2ab$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
